/**
@page setup Setup

@brief Initialise a project for a new site.

A **site** is the single source of truth for one greenhouse: its PLC payload, its
pages, its alarm table, and its config overrides. Starting a new deployment means
creating a site directory and pointing the build at it. The reference site
@ref reference "gh_mlb41" is the template to copy from.

@section setup_dir The site directory

Create `src/sites/<name>/` (the `<name>` is the code-name you select with
`-DBOTANIK_SITE`, e.g. `gh_mlb41`). A site is a small, fixed set of files:

| File | Holds |
|------|-------|
| `site.h` | The PLC payload (`PlcInputData_t` / `PlcOutputData_t` plus its status enums and their string companions) **and** the firmware subclass deriving `BotanikFirmware<>`. It also exposes the uniform handle a harness builds against: `BotanikSite`, the payload types, and the sim-only mock-PLC entry. |
| `pages.h` | The site pages (the Home and Status views for this greenhouse). |
| `alarms.h` / `alarms.cpp` | The `g_alarms[]` table - one row per alarm bit, mapping the PLC's raised bits to human-readable conditions. |
| `sim.h` | The header-only mock PLC: the data animator that fills the payload with plausible values for the simulator. Its body is guarded by `#ifdef TARGET_SIMULATOR`, so it drops out of the hardware build. |
| `config.h` | Build-wide config overrides: `#define BOTANIK_*` for any value in `libbotanik_config.h` this site needs to pin (the `LOG_PLC_*` sizes must match the PLC program). Kept separate so CMake can include it before the library defaults. |

@section setup_payload The payload contract

The site's `PlcInputData_t` / `PlcOutputData_t` is the byte-for-byte layout shared
with the M4 coprocessor; the PLC IDE generates the matching type on its side. It is
used verbatim by both the simulator's mock PLC and the OPTA firmware - never fork it
per target. Generic components constrain it (for example the alarm and status
machinery needs a 64-bit `alarms` bitset on the output struct); the site defines its
layout to satisfy those contracts and verifies the size with the `static_assert`s
noted in the simulator.

@section setup_firmware The firmware subclass

The subclass derives `BotanikFirmware<PlcInputData_t, PlcOutputData_t>` and
customises through the protected hooks rather than overriding `setup()`/`loop()`:

- `register_pages()` - the tab order (page 0 is the boot page);
- `register_commands()` - the site's shell command table;
- `on_setup()` - post-wiring done after the base is up;
- `on_loop()` - per-beat site logic.

The alarm table is passed to the base constructor. See the worked extension example
in `firmware.h`.

@section setup_build Selecting the site

The site is chosen at configure time; CMake globs `src/sites/<name>/` and points
`BOTANIK_SITE_HEADER` at its `site.h`, so the harnesses never name the site directly:

@code{.sh}
cmake -B build -DBOTANIK_TARGET=SIMULATOR -DBOTANIK_SITE=<name>
make -C build botanik_sim
@endcode

With the site building and animating under the simulator, the next step is wiring it
into the hardware project - see @ref quickstart.
*/
